Falsifies `system_tests::user::every_core_tick_budget_tests::the_backstop_bounds_a_wait_on_a_core_that_never_ticks`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect is an `EveryCoreTickBudget` with no backstop, so a wait on a core that takes no ticks
is bounded by nothing but the per-test ceiling. Another core masks its interrupts for two seconds
against a one-second backstop; without the backstop the budget ends only after that core unmasks
and takes its ticks.

Expected to fail: `assert!(budget.is_past_backstop() && STAGE.load(Ordering::SeqCst) == 1, "the
budget should have ended on its backstop with the other core still masked: {budget}")`, with no
"(the backstop)" in the message. Confirmed red on 2026-10-31 (UTC) on x86_64 at two cores with
`cargo xtask test --arch x86_64 --test the_backstop_bounds`: "4075 ms of the counter; ticks taken
of 200 on each core: core 0 407 core 1 200".

